IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cdb-core`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Act (S.C. 2023, c. 17) and Regulations (SOR/2025-35) -- from the seat of the person with a
-- disability applying for, or receiving, the Canada disability benefit. "Am I eligible this month? How much a month? Is
-- it paid as a lump sum? Do I get the $150 supplement? From when is it paid?" Facts are ones that person can state,
-- mostly from their (and their spouse's) income tax returns. The rules are in cdb-core.l4; this module builds the
-- core's records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- Unofficial; not an official version. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Canada disability benefit -- the applicant's questions`

DECLARE `CDB amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no benefit this month` HAS `because` IS A `CDB eligibility`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `turning 65` IS A BOOLEAN, `DTC` IS A BOOLEAN, `resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `status` IS A `Status in Canada`, `prison` IS AN `Incarceration`, `filed` IS A BOOLEAN, `has spouse` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse filed` IS A BOOLEAN, `waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `CDB month`
`the month from my answers` `age` `turning 65` `DTC` `resident` `status` `prison` `filed` `has spouse` `spouse filed` `waived` `suspended` MEANS
    `CDB month` WITH
        `age in years`                                              IS `age`
        `this is the month of turning 65`                           IS `turning 65`
        `is a DTC-eligible individual`                              IS `DTC`
        `resident in Canada for the Income Tax Act`                 IS `resident`
        `status`                                                    IS `status`
        `incarceration`                                             IS `prison`
        `filed a return for the last year before the payment period` IS `filed`
        `has a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`             IS `has spouse`
        `the spouse or partner filed a return for that year`        IS `spouse filed`
        `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`         IS `waived`
        `payment suspended at the beneficiary's request`            IS `suspended`

§§ `Eligibility`

@export Am I eligible for the Canada disability benefit this month (Regulations s 2)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years this month
      `I turn 65 this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the month of your 65th birthday
      `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the disability tax credit (an approved Form T2201 certificate under section 118.3 of the Income Tax Act)
      `I am resident in Canada for income tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are resident in Canada for income tax purposes
      `my status in Canada` IS A `Status in Canada` @desc One of: a Canadian citizen; a permanent resident; a temporary resident resident in Canada for the previous 18 months; a temporary resident resident in Canada for less than 18 months; a protected person; an Indian under the Indian Act; none of these
      `my incarceration` IS AN `Incarceration` @desc One of: not incarcerated; in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more, but this is the first month or the month of release; in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more
      `I filed my income tax return for last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed an income tax return for the last tax year that ended before the payment period (for July 2026 to June 2027, the 2025 return)
      `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with a spouse or common-law partner (not living apart because of a breakdown of the relationship)
      `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed an income tax return for that same year (yes if you have none)
      `the Minister waived my spouse's return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has waived the requirement for your spouse's or partner's return (for example because they live outside Canada, you live apart for reasons beyond your control, or they have been violent)
      `I asked for my payments to be suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payments are suspended this month because you asked for that in writing
GIVETH A `CDB eligibility`
`Am I eligible for the Canada disability benefit` `my age` `I turn 65 this month` `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` `I am resident in Canada for income tax` `my status in Canada` `my incarceration` `I filed my income tax return for last year` `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` `the Minister waived my spouse's return` `I asked for my payments to be suspended` MEANS
    `the allocation eligibility` (`the month from my answers` `my age` `I turn 65 this month` `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` `I am resident in Canada for income tax` `my status in Canada` `my incarceration` `I filed my income tax return for last year` `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` `the Minister waived my spouse's return` `I asked for my payments to be suspended`)

§§ `Amount`

@export How much Canada disability benefit can I get each month, after the reduction for income (Regulations s 6)?
GIVEN `the payment period begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The year in which the payment period begins (each runs from July 1 to June 30; for July 2026 to June 2027, enter 2026)
      `the CPI for 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc Statistics Canada's all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, annual average, for 2024 (not needed for the period beginning in 2025; enter any positive number)
      `the highest CPI since 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest annual average all-items CPI for any year from 2024 to the year before the payment period begins
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years this month
      `I turn 65 this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the month of your 65th birthday
      `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the disability tax credit
      `I am resident in Canada for income tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are resident in Canada for income tax purposes
      `my status in Canada` IS A `Status in Canada` @desc One of: a Canadian citizen; a permanent resident; a temporary resident resident in Canada for the previous 18 months; a temporary resident resident in Canada for less than 18 months; a protected person; an Indian under the Indian Act; none of these
      `my incarceration` IS AN `Incarceration` @desc One of: not incarcerated; in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more, but this is the first month or the month of release; in a penitentiary for a sentence of two years or more
      `I filed my income tax return for last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed an income tax return for the last tax year that ended before the payment period
      `my household` IS A `Household of the beneficiary` @desc One of: no cohabiting spouse or partner; a cohabiting spouse or partner who is not a beneficiary; a cohabiting spouse or partner who is also a beneficiary
      `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cohabiting spouse or partner filed an income tax return for that year (yes if you have none)
      `the Minister waived my spouse's return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has waived the requirement for your spouse's or partner's return
      `my own adjusted income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own net income for that tax year (line 23600), without your spouse's or partner's, in Canadian dollars
      `our adjusted family income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income plus your current cohabiting spouse's or partner's net income for that tax year (0 if you have none)
      `my working income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your employment and self-employment income for that tax year (wages, salary, and net business, farming, fishing, professional and commission income)
      `my spouse's or partner's working income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your cohabiting spouse's or partner's working income for that tax year (0 if none)
      `I asked for my payments to be suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payments are suspended this month at your request
GIVETH A `CDB amount answer`
`How much Canada disability benefit can I get` `the payment period begins in` `the CPI for 2024` `the highest CPI since 2024` `my age` `I turn 65 this month` `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` `I am resident in Canada for income tax` `my status in Canada` `my incarceration` `I filed my income tax return for last year` `my household` `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` `the Minister waived my spouse's return` `my own adjusted income` `our adjusted family income` `my working income` `my spouse's or partner's working income` `I asked for my payments to be suspended` MEANS
    LET `has spouse` MEANS NOT (`my household` EQUALS `no cohabiting spouse or partner`)
        `eligibility` MEANS `the allocation eligibility` (`the month from my answers` `my age` `I turn 65 this month` `I have an approved disability tax credit certificate` `I am resident in Canada for income tax` `my status in Canada` `my incarceration` `I filed my income tax return for last year` `has spouse` `my spouse or partner filed their return for that year` `the Minister waived my spouse's return` `I asked for my payments to be suspended`)
        `A` MEANS `the indexing factor` `the payment period begins in` `the CPI for 2024` `the highest CPI since 2024`
        `facts` MEANS `CDB income facts` WITH
                        `household`                                              IS `my household`
                        `the beneficiary's own adjusted income`                  IS `my own adjusted income`
                        `the adjusted income with the current spouse or partner` IS `our adjusted family income`
                        `the beneficiary's working income`                       IS `my working income`
                        `the spouse's or partner's working income`               IS `my spouse's or partner's working income`
                        `the Minister waived the spouse's filing condition`      IS `the Minister waived my spouse's return`
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `eligible for an allocation this month (s 2)` THEN `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is` (`the basic amount` `A` `facts`)
       OTHERWISE `no benefit this month` `eligibility`

@export Will my Canada disability benefit for the payment period be paid as one lump sum because it is $20 a month or less (Regulations s 8(2))?
GIVEN `my monthly benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly Canada disability benefit for the payment period, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my Canada disability benefit paid as a lump sum` `my monthly benefit` MEANS
    `is paid as a lump sum for the period` `my monthly benefit`

@export Can I get the $150 Canada disability benefit supplemental amount (Regulations ss 2.1, 6.1)?
GIVEN `I obtained a DTC certificate from a doctor or nurse practitioner for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained a disability tax credit certificate under paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act (the medical certificate whose cost the supplement covers)
      `an allocation was paid to me after I obtained it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Canada disability benefit payment was made to you after you obtained that certificate
      `my DTC eligibility at that payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of that payment, your disability tax credit eligibility was based on that certificate
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Can I get the $150 supplemental amount` `I obtained a DTC certificate from a doctor or nurse practitioner for this purpose` `an allocation was paid to me after I obtained it` `my DTC eligibility at that payment rests on that certificate` MEANS
    `the supplemental amount payable` `I obtained a DTC certificate from a doctor or nurse practitioner for this purpose` `an allocation was paid to me after I obtained it` `my DTC eligibility at that payment rests on that certificate`

@export How many months before the month I apply can my Canada disability benefit start (Regulations ss 5, 7)? A negative answer means after.
GIVEN `months since I first became eligible` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the month of your application you first met all the eligibility conditions (0 if only this month)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How far back can my Canada disability benefit be paid` `months since I first became eligible` MEANS
    `months before the application that the allocation starts` `months since I first became eligible`
